Subject: classify access to withheld features at the raise site

A sandbox that withholds a capability leaves its library out entirely,
so the first touch dies as "attempt to index a nil value (global
'coroutine')" -- true, and useless: nothing says the failure is policy
rather than a typo. This asks the extension, at the two places that
still hold the failing value, its kind AND its name, whether that name
is one the sandbox withholds; when it is, the raise diverts to the
extension's own error, which names the capability and is fatal.

The nil test is load-bearing: a script's own `coroutine = 5` followed
by arithmetic keeps upstream's wrong-type message, because the value
that failed is not nil. A NULL answer from the hook, a non-global kind,
or a build with the hooks off leaves every byte of the upstream path
untouched -- the check sits in the error path only, so successful
execution never runs it.

The divert happens before luaO_pushfstring allocates, and the raise
longjmps exactly where luaG_runerror would a moment later, so nothing
is stranded. Both externs live in luaext_lua_hooks.h with the others;
their definitions are src/luaext_openlibs.c (the lookup) and
src/luaext_error.c (the raise).

--- a/src/ldebug.c
+++ b/src/ldebug.c
@@ -712,6 +712,31 @@ static const char *getupvalname (CallInfo *ci, const TValue *o,
 }
 
 
+#if LUAEXT_LUA_HOOKS
+/*
+** luaext: a nil global whose name the sandbox recognises as a withheld
+** feature is not a typo, and the error should say which capability is
+** missing rather than only that the value is nil. Checked at the two places
+** that still hold the variable's name, its kind AND the failing value -- the
+** nil test is what keeps a script's own `coroutine = 5; coroutine + 1` on
+** the upstream wrong-type path. When the hook answers, the raise diverts to
+** the extension's own error, which longjmps exactly where luaG_runerror
+** would a moment later, before any message string has been built, so
+** nothing is stranded. A NULL answer, a non-global kind, a non-nil value,
+** or a build with the hooks off leaves every byte of the upstream path
+** untouched.
+*/
+static void luaext_check_withheld (lua_State *L, const TValue *o,
+                                   const char *kind, const char *name) {
+  if (ttisnil(o) && kind != NULL && strcmp(kind, "global") == 0) {
+    const char *capability = luaext_withheld_capability(L, name);
+    if (capability != NULL)
+      luaext_raise_withheld(L, name, capability);  /* does not return */
+  }
+}
+#endif
+
+
